:h1 res=2110.Help for Game
:p.
Use the :hp2.Game:ehp2. menu to start a new game, to get a hint on a good move, to quit the game or to leave the program.
:h2 res=2111.Help for New
:p.
Choose :hp2.New:ehp2. to begin a new game.
:h2 res=2112.Help for Hint
:p.
Choose :hp2.Hint:ehp2. to get a hint on a good move.
:h2 res=2130.Help for Quit Game
:p.
Choose :hp2.Quit Game:ehp2. to stop the game in progress. The board is cleared; choose :hp2.New:ehp2. to play again.
:h2 res=2131.Help for Exit
:p.
Choose :hp2.Exit:ehp2. to leave Othello. The program also ends with Ctrl+X.
:h1 res=2113.Help for Options
:p.
Use the :hp2.Options:ehp2. menu to change the level of play, to choose who starts, the background color, the sounds and the language, to hide the title bar and the menu, or to save the settings.
:h2 res=2114.Help for Beginner
:p.
Choose :hp2.Beginner:ehp2. to switch the current level of play to the Beginner level.
The higher the level of play, the longer the computer spends calculating its move.
:h2 res=2115.Help for Advanced
:p.
Choose :hp2.Advanced:ehp2. to switch the current level of play to the Advanced level.
The higher the level of play, the longer the computer spends calculating its move.
:h2 res=2116.Help for Master
:p.
Choose :hp2.Master:ehp2. to switch the current level of play to the Master level.
The higher the level of play, the longer the computer spends calculating its move.
:h2 res=2117.Help for Player starts
:p.
Choose :hp2.Player starts:ehp2. if you want to make the first move.
:h2 res=2118.Help for Computer starts
:p.
Choose :hp2.Computer starts:ehp2. if you want the Computer to make the first move.
:h2 res=16000.Help for Background color
:p.
Use the :hp2.Background color:ehp2. menu to choose a background color.
:h2 res=16001.Help for Background color
:p.
Choose this color to display the background in this color.
:h2 res=2119.Help for Sound
:p.
Choose :hp2.Sound:ehp2. to display a dialog window that lets you assign sounds to events.
:h3 res=13510.Help for Sound dialog
:p.
Select :hp2.Sound:ehp2. to activate sound for events.
:p.
The events list contains the names of all events you can assign sounds to.
:p.
The sounds list contains the names of all available sound files as well as an entry <No sound> and <Beep>. To assign a sound to an event, select the event first and then double-click on the sound that you want to assign.
:p.
Use the :hp2.Volume:ehp2. slider to set the sound volume.
:p.
The :hp2.Play (>):ehp2. button plays the currently selected sound.
:p.
The :hp2.OK:ehp2. button closes the Sound dialog and the changed settings become active.
:p.
The :hp2.Cancel:ehp2. button closes the Sound dialog. Any changes that were made are discarded.
:h2 res=2132.Help for Language
:p.
Choose :hp2.Language:ehp2. to select English, Spanish, Dutch, German, French or Italian. The menus, the messages and this help change at once, and the language is remembered.
:h2 res=2133.Help for Save settings on exit
:p.
Choose :hp2.Save settings on exit:ehp2. to keep the level, the player who starts, the background color, the sound settings and the language for the next time. The check mark shows that the settings will be saved.
:h2 res=2134.Help for Frame Controls
:p.
Choose :hp2.Frame Controls:ehp2. (Ctrl+F) to hide the title bar and the menu, which leaves only the board. Press Ctrl+F again to bring them back.
:h1 res=2120.Help for Help
:p.
Use the :hp2.Help:ehp2. menu to obtain help information.
:h2 res=2124.Help for Help index
:p.
Choose :hp2.Help index:ehp2. to display the help index. The help index lists the titles of the help information that is available.
:h2 res=2122.Help for General help
:p.
Choose :hp2.General help:ehp2. to get general help for the program. General help provides general information about Othello.
:h2 res=2123.Help for Keys help
:p.
Choose :hp2.Keys help:ehp2. to see a list of keys and a description of the function of the keys.
:h3 res=2129.Keys help
:i1.Keys help
:p.:hp2.CONTROL KEYS:ehp2.
:dl break=all.
:dt.Arrow keys
:dd.Move you around the board in the direction of the arrow.
:dt.Enter, Spacebar, Return
:dd.Places a marker.
:dt.Ctrl+N
:dd.Starts a new game.
:dt.Ctrl+H
:dd.Gets a hint.
:dt.Ctrl+Q
:dd.Quits the game in progress.
:dt.Ctrl+F
:dd.Hides or shows the title bar and the menu.
:dt.Ctrl+X
:dd.Exits the program.
:edl.
:p.:hp2.HELP KEYS:ehp2.
:dl break=all.
:dt.F1
:dd.Gets help.
:dt.Esc
:dd.Views previous Help panel or ends help if only one panel has been viewed.
:dt.Alt+F4
:dd.Ends help or ends program.
:edl.
:p.:hp2.SYSTEM KEYS:ehp2.
:dl break=all.
:dt.Alt+Esc
:dd.Switches to the next program.
:dt.Ctrl+Esc
:dd.Switches to the Window List.
:edl.
:p.:hp2.WINDOW KEYS:ehp2.
:dl break=all.
:dt.Underlined letter
:dd.Moves among the choices on the action bar and pull-downs submenu or executes the function chosen.
:dt.Alt+Underlined letter
:dd.Executes the function chosen immediately.
:edl.
:h2 res=2121.Help for Using help
:p.
Choose :hp2.Using help:ehp2. to obtain information on how to use the Help facility.
:h2 res=2125.Help for Product information
:p.
Choose :hp2.About:ehp2. to view a dialog that displays information about Othello, such as version number and copyright notice.
:h3 res=3100.Help for Product information dialog
:p.
This dialog displays information about Othello, such as version number and copyright notice.
:p.
The :hp2.Close:ehp2. button closes the product information dialog.
:euserdoc.
